Input: {"question": "Which award did Ernest Beutler receive?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 14, "text": "Ernest Beutler"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 16, "end": 203, "text": "Ernest Beutler (1928-2008) was an American hematologist who made significant contributions to the field of hematology, particularly in the area of red blood cell metabolism and disorders."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 204, "end": 228, "text": "Early Life and Education"}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 230, "end": 288, "text": "Beutler was born on August 13, 1928, in Chicago, Illinois."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 289, "end": 463, "text": "He received his undergraduate degree from the University of Chicago and went on to earn his medical degree from the University of Chicago Pritzker School of Medicine in 1952."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 464, "end": 470, "text": "Career"}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 472, "end": 642, "text": "Beutler completed his internship and residency at the University of Chicago Hospitals and later served as a research associate at the National Institutes of Health (NIH)."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 643, "end": 823, "text": "In 1962, he joined the faculty at the University of California, San Diego, where he established the Division of Hematology and became a prominent figure in the field of hematology."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 824, "end": 851, "text": "Contributions to Hematology"}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 853, "end": 1017, "text": "Beutler's research focused on red blood cell metabolism and disorders, including glucose-6-phosphate dehydrogenase (G6PD) deficiency and pyruvate kinase deficiency."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1018, "end": 1147, "text": "He made significant contributions to the understanding of these disorders and developed diagnostic tests and treatments for them."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1148, "end": 1165, "text": "Awards and Honors"}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1167, "end": 1298, "text": "Beutler received numerous awards and honors for his contributions to hematology, including the Canada Gairdner International Award."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1299, "end": 1334, "text": "Canada Gairdner International Award"}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1336, "end": 1460, "text": "The Canada Gairdner International Award is a prestigious award that recognizes outstanding contributions to medical science."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1461, "end": 1635, "text": "Established in 1959, the award is presented annually by the Gairdner Foundation to scientists who have made significant discoveries or contributions to the field of medicine."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1636, "end": 1703, "text": "Ernest Beutler's Receipt of the Canada Gairdner International Award"}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1705, "end": 1848, "text": "In 1975, Ernest Beutler was awarded the Canada Gairdner International Award for his pioneering work on red blood cell metabolism and disorders."}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1849, "end": 2004, "text": "This award is a testament to his significant contributions to the field of hematology and his impact on the understanding and treatment of blood disorders."}, "D1S20": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2005, "end": 2016, "text": "References:"}, "D1S21": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2018, "end": 2052, "text": "* \"Ernest Beutler, MD, 1928-2008\"."}, "D1S22": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2053, "end": 2084, "text": "American Society of Hematology."}, "D1S23": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2085, "end": 2106, "text": "Retrieved 2022-02-20."}, "D1S24": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2107, "end": 2147, "text": "* \"Canada Gairdner International Award\"."}, "D1S25": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2148, "end": 2168, "text": "Gairdner Foundation."}, "D1S26": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2169, "end": 2190, "text": "Retrieved 2022-02-20."}, "D1S27": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2191, "end": 2210, "text": "* \"Ernest Beutler\"."}, "D1S28": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2211, "end": 2240, "text": "National Academy of Sciences."}, "D1S29": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2241, "end": 2262, "text": "Retrieved 2022-02-20."}, "D1S30": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2263, "end": 2283, "text": "* \"Beutler, Ernest\"."}, "D1S31": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2284, "end": 2305, "text": "Who's Who in America."}, "D1S32": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2306, "end": 2324, "text": "Marquis Who's Who."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 18, "text": "**Ernest Beutler**"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 20, "end": 161, "text": "Ernest Beutler (1928-2008) was an American hematologist and medical researcher who made significant contributions to the field of hematology."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 162, "end": 310, "text": "Born in Chicago, Illinois, Beutler earned his medical degree from the University of Chicago and went on to pursue a career in research and academia."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 311, "end": 340, "text": "**Early Career and Research**"}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 342, "end": 454, "text": "Beutler's early research focused on the study of red blood cell metabolism and the diagnosis of blood disorders."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 455, "end": 563, "text": "His work led to the development of new diagnostic tests and treatments for various hematological conditions."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 564, "end": 732, "text": "In the 1960s, Beutler joined the faculty at the University of California, San Diego, where he established the Hematology Division and served as its director until 1985."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 733, "end": 754, "text": "**Literary Pursuits**"}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 756, "end": 839, "text": "In addition to his work in hematology, Beutler was an accomplished writer and poet."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 840, "end": 928, "text": "His literary works often explored themes of medicine, science, and the human experience."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 929, "end": 1067, "text": "Beutler's writing was widely praised for its lyricism and depth, and he was recognized with several literary awards for his contributions."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1068, "end": 1117, "text": "**Asian\\/Pacific American Awards for Literature**"}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1119, "end": 1250, "text": "In 1995, Beutler received the Asian\\/Pacific American Awards for Literature (APALA) for his poetry collection, \"The Blood of Life.\""}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1251, "end": 1347, "text": "This prestigious award recognizes outstanding literary works by Asian\\/Pacific American authors."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1348, "end": 1471, "text": "Beutler's win marked a significant milestone in his literary career, as he was the first hematologist to receive the award."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id"